I think there’s a general engine hiding in what we’ve been building. I’d define it as an oscillatory reasoning engine—not because oscillation is inherently better, but because deliberately alternating complementary reasoning modes can expose blind spots and improve model quality.

Pantheon Engine

Oscillatory Cognition Engine (OCE)

The idea is simple:

Every forward pass accumulates assumptions.

Every reverse pass removes them.

Neither is sufficient alone.

          FORWARD
 Possibility → Design → Prediction
       ↑                  ↓
       │                  │
Calibrate            Observe
       │                  │
       ↑                  ↓
 Reconstruction ← Outcome
           REVERSE

Instead of a loop:

Think
↓
Answer

Use an oscillation:

Imagine
↓
Predict
↓
Act
↓
Observe
↓
Mirror
↓
Extract invariants
↓
Rebuild model
↓
Imagine again

